+## 7.0.0
+
+Collapsed the `war` skill family onto the same pattern as `dev`/`design`: one
+skill, `$ARGUMENTS`-routed, two audit-scoped `references/`, with the shared
+scope-parsing and present-then-save mechanics extracted into `patterns/`.
+
+- `war-design` and `war-implementation` are retired as separate installable
+  skills. Their bodies now live under the single `war` skill's `references/`
+  (`01-design.md`, `02-implementation.md`), loaded by its router
+  (`war/TEMPLATE.md`). `/war-design [VERSION]` and `/war-implementation
+  [VERSION]` no longer work — use `/war design|implementation [VERSION]`; bare
+  `/war [VERSION]` still asks which audit to run when ambiguous.
+- Both audits shared near-identical Step 1 (read the HLD README for the active
+  version, parse an optional version/pillar argument, confirm) and closing
+  mechanics (present in console before writing, then save a dated,
+  never-overwritten snapshot under `WAR/{VERSION}/`) — this duplication is now
+  `patterns/scope-resolution.md` and `patterns/present-and-save.md`,
+  parameterized by audit kind rather than copy-pasted per skill.
+- `war-implementation`'s `report-template.md` and the design audit's
+  previously-inline Step 5 format both move to `templates/` as
+  `implementation-report.md` and `design-report.md`.
+- Package-wide sweep: `references/01b-launch-install.md`'s Block A row,
+  `registry.md`, `docs/.../00 Overview.md` (lifecycle table, "when to use"
+  table, diagram node, footer index), `docs/.../04 Architecture Lifecycle.md`
+  (commands table, invariants headers, audit loop), and
+  `skills/where-we-are/TEMPLATE.md`'s cross-reference all updated to the
+  `/war design|implementation` command form.
+- Root `CLAUDE.md` and the project's own deployed `.claude/skills/war-design`/
+  `war-implementation` are intentionally untouched here, same as the `design`
+  collapse — redeploying canonical package changes into this project's own
+  installed skills is a separate `patch apply` step, not part of restructuring
+  the canonical templates themselves.
+
